# Code Style Rules

## General Guidelines
- Follow RuboCop Rails conventions
- Keep methods small and focused (ideally under 10 lines)
- Use proper naming conventions
- Document complex methods
- Maintain consistent formatting

## Parameter Usage
- Use named parameters over positional parameters
- Group related parameters together
- Provide default values when appropriate
- Document parameter types and requirements

## Method Design
- Single responsibility principle
- Clear, descriptive method names
- Consistent return types
- Proper error handling
- Appropriate method visibility

## Examples

✅ Correct:
```ruby
# Using named parameters with defaults
def create_user(name:, email:, role: :user, metadata: {})
  # ...
end

# Small, focused method
def calculate_discount(subtotal:, tax_rate:)
  subtotal * (1 + tax_rate)
end

# Well-documented complex method
# @param [Array<Integer>] numbers List of numbers to process
# @return [Hash] Statistics about the numbers
def calculate_statistics(numbers)
  # ...
end
```

❌ Incorrect:
- Positional parameters without clear meaning
- Long, complex methods
- Inconsistent naming
- Poor documentation
- Mixed return types
